# AGENTS.md — {{ project.name }}

Pilot's checklist, not a style guide. Every line lands in the system prompt on every turn and
competes for attention with every other line. Under 60 lines.

**Each rule should end with the run that earned it.** No run id means it was brainstormed
rather than ratcheted — delete it.

## Project

- {{ project.description }} [seed]
- One unit of work: {{ goal.unit }} [seed]

## Hard boundaries

- Never edit anything matched by `gate.yaml: deny`. Those files are what you are judged
  against. Editing them is not a shortcut, it is a hard stop that pages a human. [seed]
- Never add a suppression — `skip`, `xfail`, `# type: ignore`, `# noqa` — to clear a gate.
  Fix the finding or report that you cannot. [seed]
- Never loosen a threshold or tolerance to make a check pass. [seed]

## Working style

- Read `STATE.md` first, every run. It is the only thing that survives your context. [seed]
- Run `{{ verify.command }}` before claiming done. A claim is not evidence. [seed]
- One goal per run. Log unrelated findings under `## Observed, not actioned` in `STATE.md`
  rather than fixing them. [seed]
- If the same gate fails twice with identical text, stop and say what is underspecified. A
  third identical attempt trips the no-progress rule and wastes the run. Being stuck is
  information. [seed]
- Update `STATE.md` before you finish. The next attempt is a fresh context with no memory of
  this one, and that file is all it inherits. [seed]

